{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-ns-obstruction-computation-asymptotic","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Remark","doco:Section"],"label":"rem:ns-obstruction-computation-asymptotic","kind":"remark","title":"Formal asymptotic content of the jet divergence","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-surreal-blowup-calculus","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-standard-part-functor","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-conway-normal-form","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-body-asymptotics-catalog"],"interprets":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-ns-obstruction-computation","tags":["navier-stokes","asymptotics","surreal","blowup"],"text":"ns-obstruction-computation-asymptotic.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"rem:ns-obstruction-computation-asymptotic\"></a><p>The absolute jet divergence <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">|j^n v|_\\Sigma \\sim 1/(T^*-t)^{(n+1)/2}</code> translates into <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\ordw(\\lvert j^n v \\rvert_\\Sigma) = -\\tfrac{n+1}{2}\\,\\ordw(T^*-t)</code> as <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">t \\to T^*</code>. The complete recursive jet tower establishes the <a href=\"#def:surreal-blowup-calculus\">surreal blow-up calculus</a>, while the exact <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q \\to 1</code> classical-limit extraction requires the <a href=\"#def:standard-part-functor\">standard-part map</a>. See also <a href=\"#rem:conway-normal-form\">Big-O via <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\ordw</code></a> alongside the <a href=\"#rem:body-asymptotics-catalog\">body asymptotics catalog</a>.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/ns-obstruction-computation-asymptotic.md","heading":"Remark","number":"19.6.4"}
